00:58:52.560 --> 00:58:53.977
that, "Oh, there it is.

00:58:53.977 --> 00:58:55.020
"He just lost the game."

00:58:55.020 --> 00:58:57.200
He just made a critical mistake,

00:58:57.200 --> 00:59:00.293
he'd get this look on his
face like I've blown it.

00:59:01.166 --> 00:59:01.999
You know what I'm saying.

00:59:01.999 --> 00:59:03.200
He's like, he wants to win so bad.

00:59:03.200 --> 00:59:07.160
And it's just like, it's
only, and this is a flaw.

00:59:07.160 --> 00:59:09.340
This is something that I've had to,

00:59:09.340 --> 00:59:13.840
I continue to work on is
like, are you having fun

00:59:13.840 --> 00:59:14.773
if you don't win.

00:59:16.360 --> 00:59:19.010
Super competitive people
have trouble having fun

00:59:19.010 --> 00:59:19.870
if they don't,

00:59:19.870 --> 00:59:21.450
if they're not winning.

00:59:21.450 --> 00:59:23.810
If they're doing something
and they're like,

00:59:23.810 --> 00:59:25.400
I'm not good at this.

00:59:25.400 --> 00:59:27.990
And I don't think I'm gonna
be able to be good enough

00:59:27.990 --> 00:59:29.633
at this to be competitive in it.

00:59:30.878 --> 00:59:32.120
So I'm gonna lose interest.

00:59:32.120 --> 00:59:34.810
And so those are the kind of factors,

00:59:34.810 --> 00:59:38.970
but I think the fact that
everybody wants to win ultimately

00:59:38.970 --> 00:59:40.990
is how you get people roped
into games in my family.

00:59:40.990 --> 00:59:43.867
But we started quarantine with games

00:59:43.867 --> 00:59:45.500
and they've completely fallen off.

00:59:45.500 --> 00:59:49.010
Like we were playing Scrabble.

00:59:49.010 --> 00:59:50.603
I mean, we were scrabbling it up.

00:59:50.603 --> 00:59:52.500
I've never played Scrabble.

00:59:52.500 --> 00:59:54.240
Again, that's odd to me,

00:59:54.240 --> 00:59:56.740
that you haven't run across a Scrabble.

