01:07:39.370 --> 01:07:41.350
Or I'll the person who's not.

01:07:41.350 --> 01:07:44.580
And then it's a Debbie
Downer, it destroys it.

01:07:44.580 --> 01:07:48.890
So when you do something well
and don't think about it,

01:07:48.890 --> 01:07:50.930
I think you're also isolating it to games,

01:07:50.930 --> 01:07:53.093
but like anything, well,

01:07:54.240 --> 01:07:56.180
anything that you do in your career,

01:07:56.180 --> 01:07:58.410
like I'm trying to do this well,

01:07:58.410 --> 01:08:01.450
I'm trying to be a certain way about this.

01:08:01.450 --> 01:08:04.220
I'm trying to create this piece of,

01:08:04.220 --> 01:08:06.780
I guess my definition of competition

01:08:06.780 --> 01:08:10.590
is just much wider as well,
because what I'm saying is

01:08:10.590 --> 01:08:13.140
I feel like competitiveness

01:08:14.750 --> 01:08:17.370
is one of the elements that has gotten us

01:08:17.370 --> 01:08:19.380
to where we're at in our career.

01:08:19.380 --> 01:08:20.910
Like, and it is, I don't mean like,

01:08:20.910 --> 01:08:23.710
Ooh, I want to get more views
than this other channel.

01:08:23.710 --> 01:08:25.463
I mean, sometimes it
might come down to that,

01:08:25.463 --> 01:08:26.296
but it's not really that.

01:08:26.296 --> 01:08:28.330
It's more like I'm
competing against myself.

01:08:28.330 --> 01:08:33.330
Like ultimately everybody wants
to be important in some way.

01:08:33.810 --> 01:08:36.230
And people who are in their entertainment

01:08:36.230 --> 01:08:38.990
kind of achieve that
and find their purpose

01:08:38.990 --> 01:08:43.940
a lot of times in, eliciting
a reaction from people.

01:08:43.940 --> 01:08:46.830
And I would say that you are actually

01:08:46.830 --> 01:08:51.830
even more focused and
committed to getting a reaction

01:08:53.490 --> 01:08:57.130
from a crowd or from an
individual than I am.

01:08:57.130 --> 01:08:59.530
You think about, like the
way that you're super,

01:09:00.434 --> 01:09:02.573
I'm much less concerned about things like,

01:09:03.510 --> 01:09:05.890
where is this thing and
where is the camera?

01:09:05.890 --> 01:09:09.510
And am I showing, am I opening
this box in the right way?

01:09:09.510 --> 01:09:12.280
In my mind, that's all competitive nature.

01:09:12.280 --> 01:09:16.980
It's like, you have a commitment
to excellence and you may,

01:09:16.980 --> 01:09:18.290
you're thinking about competitiveness

01:09:18.290 --> 01:09:23.200
in like I'm throwing a ball
faster than a person or not,

01:09:23.200 --> 01:09:26.870
but like, you actually care
about that stuff more than I do.

01:09:26.870 --> 01:09:31.270
And I would call that sort of purse.

01:09:31.270 --> 01:09:34.330
I would almost say it's
a relentless pursuit

01:09:34.330 --> 01:09:36.370
of doing things in a certain way.

01:09:36.370 --> 01:09:38.123
Perfection is not, I mean,

01:09:39.348 --> 01:09:43.077
is attained by comparison
to like a standard.

01:09:46.660 --> 01:09:49.290
But I think it's a stretch to
say that that's competition,

01:09:49.290 --> 01:09:51.290
like I'm competing against the standard.

01:09:53.450 --> 01:09:56.933
I also think it is, I think
it's a little muddied by,

01:09:58.750 --> 01:09:59.583
I don't know.

01:10:01.014 --> 01:10:03.520
Do you do you get from
me in this conversation

01:10:03.520 --> 01:10:06.950
that like I judge you
for being competitive?

01:10:06.950 --> 01:10:07.783
Yes.

01:10:10.730 --> 01:10:14.320
Okay, so we're breaking in Kiko,

01:10:14.320 --> 01:10:17.820
I don't envy what the
decisions you've had to make

01:10:17.820 --> 01:10:22.320
in editing this, but apparently
Kiko has decided that

01:10:22.320 --> 01:10:27.090
what you just heard was
like the truncated point

01:10:27.090 --> 01:10:29.507
and the end of this episode--

01:10:30.943 --> 01:10:31.776
And the reason being--

01:10:31.776 --> 01:10:35.090
And then next week, you'll
get the continuation

01:10:35.090 --> 01:10:38.960
